# Low-Level Curriculum Command Center - Zero-to-One Architecture

This document answers the immediate directives to outline the architecture, schema, directory structure, and foundational bootstrapping code for the highly specialized technical learning platform.

## 1. The Tech Stack

- **Backend Framework**: **Python FastAPI**. It is lightning-fast, exceptionally efficient for local setups, and intrinsically supports deep data validation via Pydantic — crucial for heavily constrained, nested payload handling. 
- **Database / Data Store**: **SQLite + SQLAlchemy + Alembic**. An embedded SQLite database (`app.db`) enables frictionless deployment requiring no external heavy servers. SQLAlchemy handles the deeply nested CRUD operations elegantly.
- **Frontend Core**: **React via Vite** (TypeScript). Vite provides a highly performant local dev environment to build out the front end rapidly.
- **Styling**: **Vanilla CSS / CSS Modules**. Strict adherence to a custom Cyberpunk design system (using CSS Variables) without heavy utility-class abstractions like Tailwind, ensuring ultimate granular control over the UI, dark surfaces, neon accents, and heavy terminal outputs.
- **State Management & Fetching**: **React Query (TanStack Query)**. It automatically binds to React components, making UI updates frictionless without page reloads after interacting with the local backend CMS.

## 2. The Data Schema

The data model embraces a deeply nested structure, implemented precisely across Pydantic schemas and SQLAlchemy models:

```mermaid
erDiagram
    SPRINT ||--o{ PROJECT : contains
    SPRINT {
        int id
        string title
        string description
    }
    PROJECT ||--o{ TASK : contains
    PROJECT {
        int id
        int sprint_id
        string title
        string directory_name
        text global_constraints
        text forbidden_functions
    }
    TASK {
        int id
        int project_id
        string title
        string task_type
        text technical_requirements
        text raw_terminal_output
        boolean is_completed
    }
```

- **Sprint**: The macro container (e.g., "Low-Level Programming v2").
- **Project**: Represents a specific repository/unit (e.g., "0x09. C - Strace"). Holds heavy global constraints.
- **Task**: Granular assignments (e.g., "0. Syscall Name", "1. Syscall args"). Contains raw valgrind/ptrace output strings that demand perfect preservation.

